I had problems with this as well; what I had to do was change what my
TERM environment variable was set to, from "xterm" to "xterm-color".
The method that works for me so I can change it only for this is to
just stick it in front of my ssh command (so my command line is
'TERM="xterm-color" ssh araltaln@nethack1.devnull.net', or whatever
other server I connect to); I imagine you could stick 'set
TERM="xterm-color"' in your .bashrc or similar to just keep it changed.
I don't know of any gui-based way of doing this, but would love to hear
about one.

